#{[17592186531621 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531621 #edb/ref 1069 "q-138022" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531621 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531621 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531621 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "957651b3-45e4-5a93-853b-1785322d0942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531621 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}^{2}\\le {x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So,  in turn, $Q(x)\\le 1.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $1.$ But before we conclude that $1$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=1.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(1)^{2}-(0)^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531663 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "085cdc0b-e1a7-5229-892c-0ef2ac49749e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531663 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531686 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186531708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531686 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "46e11e28-122a-5f86-8bf2-7977b37760ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531686 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186269162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531690 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186531663 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531690 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "66cbd984-34bf-5c4b-b040-16117bac09ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531690 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186269171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218